Z||000000||FieroFanaticus2||05-28-2001||07:06 AM||||Ok, here's what happens.  When I drive somewhere it runs/drives great.  Then I get there and shut the engine off.  When I go to restart the engine, the first try always fails - it just cranks, so I turn the key back to the off position, try again and it starts up.  BUT if I give it a little gas during the first try it'll choke a little and start up for me.  My idle will also bounce from 400 - 1200 until I put it into first and start driving.  AND when slowing down to a stop from 55 MPH or so  downshifting the check engine light will come on either until I get it into 2nd gear downshifting, or into 2nd from the stop.<BR>Does anybody have any clue what this could be?  ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Fierowrecker||05-28-2001||07:23 AM||||I would think it to be the TPS or MAP in that order...<BR>crash...||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroFanaticus2||05-28-2001||09:08 AM||||What's the TPS?  I know what and where the MAP is, but have never heard of TSP.  I have the Chilton repair book, but can't find that anywhere in it.||||reg||1
