Z||000004||tgowens||05-28-2001||01:42 PM||||TPS is the throttle position sensor and it is located on the throttle body right above the IAC (idle air control).<P>Also, check the connections on the top of the coil and make sure they haven't come loose.....||||reg||1
Z||000005||FieroFanaticus2||07-01-2001||02:46 PM||||Ok, I have replaced the TPS and MAP Sensor.<BR>NOW, when I start the car it Idles at around 2000 for a few seconds, then slowly drops to around 1200.  When I drive and push in the clutch it will drop to around 400, but not always.  It even dies sometimes while I am downshifting (has done this 3 or 4 times).  The Check Engine Light comes on once in a while too.  The PCV line is fine on both ends.  Could it be the IAC valve doing this?<BR>Someone had mentioned once before that it could be the MAT Sensor, but I can't find any information on that in my book.  What is the MAT sensor?  In order to replace that am I going to need to relieve the fuel pressure and also drain the coolant?<BR>Your info is appreciated.||||reg||1
